+# Expanding the ROM
+
+Mod-branch notes for growing this disassembly beyond the retail image. `main` keeps byte-identical builds against the supported ROM revisions.
+
+## What the build does
+
+- `src/hockey93.asm` fills to **512 KB** (`dcb.b $80000-*,$FF`). Includes **after** that fill start at `$80000`, so retail addresses below the fill do not move.
+- `CHECKSUM=0` (`build:dev` / per-revision dev modes) skips boot validation while iterating.
+- If SNASM reports **Branch (… bytes) is out of range**, `tools/build.js` prints a hint and points here.
+
+## Short jumps and PC-relative branches
+
+SNASM’s **Branch (n bytes) is out of range** is the ~±32 KB limit on **PC-relative** branches: **`bsr.w`**, **`bra.w`**, and **`bxx.w`**.
+
+Fix, in order of preference:
+
+1. Put new ROM **after the 512 KB fill** in `src/hockey93.asm`.
+2. Do not insert new code **between** existing includes if later modules are branched to with `.w` (only a small shift can break a branch that was already near the limit).
+3. From retail code into post-fill code, use **`jsr (label).l`** / **`jmp (label).l`**. In new post-fill code, use **`.l`** or a **local `rts`** instead of **`bsr.w`** to distant labels.
+
+General team tables, save RAM, and mapper notes for later NHL Genesis titles are documented in [NHL94Genesis `docs/EXPANDING_THE_ROM.md`](https://github.com/abdulahmad/NHL94Genesis/blob/main/docs/EXPANDING_THE_ROM.md) where they apply to your mod.
diff --git a/tools/assembleHints.js b/tools/assembleHints.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..546b35e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/assembleHints.js
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+'use strict';
+
+// Helpers for SNASM68k assemble failures. Used by tools/build.js.
+
+const DEFAULT_DOC = 'docs/EXPANDING_THE_ROM.md';
+
+function filterAssemblerErrors(lines) {
+    return lines.filter((l) => /\.(asm|inc|mac)\(\d+|error|fatal|not recognised|undefined|could not/i.test(l) && !/error\(s\) from/.test(l)).slice(0, 40);
+}
+
+function hasBranchOutOfRange(lines) {
+    const text = (Array.isArray(lines) ? lines : [lines]).join('\n');
+    return /branch\s*\([^)]*\)\s*is out of range/i.test(text)
+        || (/out of range/i.test(text) && /branch/i.test(text));
+}
+
+function expandingRomBranchHint(options = {}) {
+    const doc = options.doc || DEFAULT_DOC;
+    const fill = options.fillHint || 'the stock ROM fill in the top-level .asm include list';
+    return [
+        '',
+        'Branch out of range (68000 PC-relative limit ~±32 KB):',
+        `  • Do not insert new ROM between existing modules if later code is branched to with .w — put new data after ${fill}.`,
+        '  • From retail code into post-fill code, use jsr (label).l / jmp (label).l.',
+        '  • In new post-fill code, use .l calls or a local rts instead of bsr.w to distant labels.',
+        `  • Read ${doc} (Short jumps — PC-relative branches).`,
+    ].join('\n');
+}
+
+function formatAssemblerFailureDetail(lines, options = {}) {
+    let detail = filterAssemblerErrors(lines).join('\n');
+    if (hasBranchOutOfRange(lines)) detail += expandingRomBranchHint(options);
+    return detail;
+}
+
+module.exports = {
+    DEFAULT_DOC,
+    filterAssemblerErrors,
+    hasBranchOutOfRange,
+    expandingRomBranchHint,
+    formatAssemblerFailureDetail,
+};
